---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Challenge & Staking Rules — StreakGrid"
  description="Comprehensive documentation of how StreakGrid evaluates daily success, deadlines, streaks, and proof."
>
  <div class="legal-page-layout">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <div class="legal-header-inner">
        <a href="/" class="brand-link">
          <div class="brand-badge">✓</div>
          <span class="brand-name">StreakGrid</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">Return Home</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="legal-content-container">
      <div class="legal-doc-card">
        <div class="doc-header">
          <span class="doc-tag">Official Rules</span>
          <h1 class="doc-title">Challenge & Accountability Rules</h1>
          <span class="doc-date">Version 2.0 • Published September 2026</span>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-body">
          <section class="doc-section">
            <h2>1. The Daily Deadline</h2>
            <p>
              Every challenge tracks calendar days sequentially from Day 1 to the configured duration (30, 50, or 100 days).
            </p>
            <p>
              Daily evaluation occurs according to the challenge's configured timezone (stored in UTC). A day closes precisely at <strong>23:59:59</strong>. Once a day has elapsed into the past, uncompleted pending cells are marked as missed.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="doc-section">
            <h2>2. What Counts as a Successful Day</h2>
            <p>
              During challenge creation, the user selects one of three immutable success rules:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Complete all activities:</strong> All active tracker columns must be checked for the day to count as successful.</li>
              <li><strong>Complete at least one activity:</strong> Checking any single activity completes the day and preserves the streak.</li>
              <li><strong>Custom minimum count:</strong> A defined number of activities (e.g. at least 3 of 5) must be completed each day.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              Exempt activities (marked with «—») are excluded from the required denominator for that day.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="doc-section">
            <h2>3. Streak Calculation & Grace Logic</h2>
            <p>
              Streaks represent consecutive successful calendar days:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>If Today is completed, the streak includes Today and extends backward.</li>
              <li>If Today is still in progress (pending), your current streak reflects consecutive successful days up through Yesterday.</li>
              <li>A single missed past day resets the active streak counter to zero, but your total successful days and consistency percentage remain preserved.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section class="doc-section">
            <h2>4. What Happens on Success vs Failure</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Success:</strong> Achieving the target consistency rate unlocks permanent completion badges (e.g. <em>100 DAY SHIPPER</em>) and initiates immediate full refund of your refundable deposit.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Failure:</strong> If consistency targets are not met, the challenge concludes respectfully as incomplete, and the deposit is forfeited according to the locked terms.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section class="doc-section">
            <h2>5. Proof of Work (Build in Public & Output Challenges)</h2>
            <p>
              For public challenges such as <em>100 Days Build in Public</em>, users are encouraged to attach a short completion summary and project URL (e.g., live product link, open source repository, or public documentation). Heavy file uploads are avoided to keep the platform fast and privacy-friendly.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page-layout {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--color-bg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .legal-header {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 12px 20px;
  }

  .legal-header-inner {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .brand-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .brand-badge {
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    background: var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: 5px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .legal-content-container {
    max-width: 860px;
    width: 100%;
    margin: 30px auto 80px auto;
    padding: 0 20px;
  }

  .legal-doc-card {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-modal);
    padding: 40px 36px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  .doc-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .doc-tag {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-primary-hover);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .doc-title {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .doc-date {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .doc-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .doc-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .doc-section h2 {
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .doc-section ul {
    margin-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
</style>
